content.text:
Fixed. The contact page's "Other ways to reach us" card had lost the ability to wrap its long support email address (`customer.support.team@acmestorefront.example`), so the text spilled out of the card — and on phones it widened the whole page from 390px to 424px, causing a horizontal scrollbar and shifting the layout.

**Fix** — `site/css/pages.css:253`:

```css
.info-list dd {
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}
```

`anywhere` rather than `break-word` matters here: the card sits in a `1fr` grid track, whose automatic minimum is the content's min-content width. Only `anywhere` reduces that min-content size, so the page stops overflowing on narrow screens.

**Verification** — full suite passes, 28/28 (16 functional + 12 visual), including the contact screenshots at both desktop and phone sizes. Only `site/css/pages.css` changed.

STATUS: DONE

